  <Folder><name>Confirmed in the field (18)</name><description><![CDATA[Fixed by something said or walked in the field, recorded in place_aliases.csv with the reason.]]></description><open>0</open>
    <Placemark><name>Aguido</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM: Aguido Primary School, 200 m from where the route implied. The recording 'Vereyame connects Yoivi, Aguido Primary School and Kuheine' names it, so R02 is already walked]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.449290,-9.141040,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Asafa</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village 15 km WNW of Gora. (An Asafa 406 km away in Eastern Highlands was rejected)]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.106970,-8.976760,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Babarobo</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village, and it sits almost exactly on the Biriri-Safia line, which is the leg the list puts it in]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.522630,-9.356620,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Buangfu</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>CONFIRMED by Will, 18 Oct 2026 as a hamlet of Kokoro, spelled Buamfu by him and Buangfu in Russell's file. Position is the START of '2026-08-07 12:14 Buangfu to Kuai trek' - again a track endpoint, 1.41 km from the Kokoro waypoint and 0.59 km from Jakiro]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.267910,-9.178010,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Damara</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>FOUND 18 Oct 2026 in the MCA waypoint file as 'Damara Village' - see waypoints_mca.csv. One of the five places that blocked a whole route for want of a position; F47 Damara-Bua can now be checked]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.440060,-9.130250,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Embi</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village south of Dobodura - the longitude that was missing on 3 Oct. Sits 1.7 km from Warisota, which is the next place in the same route. (Mount Embi 656 km away in Enga was rejected)]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.430600,-8.837290,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Jakiro</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>CONFIRMED by Will, 18 Oct 2026: a hamlet of Kokoro. Position is the END of Russell's '2026-08-07 10:53 Trek from Anatua to Jakiro', so it is where he stopped walking, not a surveyed point - 0.87 km from the Kokoro waypoint. Not in the MCA waypoint file, which names Namieta and Maragane as hamlets of Kokoro but not this one]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.268070,-9.172710,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Kiara</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>FLIPPED by Will, 16 Oct 2026: Kiara is the correct name and the gazetteer spelling Kiera is the error - the reverse of what was recorded on 3 Oct, when only the two spellings being one place was settled. Still NOT Kira. The position is the gazetteer's surveyed one, so nothing moves; the GPS-inferred Kiara cluster 513 m NW is not used, the survey outranking our own inference]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.288200,-9.095910,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Kwikila</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>CONFIRMED by Will, 4 Oct 2026: correct, and it is an old foot track. The Rigo District station in Central Province (geodatos.net), 75 km SW of Jaure]]></description><Point><coordinates>147.659680,-9.818470,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Ombara</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>confirmed by Will, 3 Oct 2026: Umbara is NOT Umbuara. The eastern Ombara, fixed by the Kuheine-Umbara trail endpoint]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.467500,-9.136200,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Oro Bay</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>PUBLIC SOURCE (Pacific Wrecks, 8d53'41\S 148d29'25\"E): the coastal town. H01 Orobay-Itokama then reads as the highway from the coast up to Itokama - confirm this is meant"]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.490280,-8.894720,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Peroroda</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village. 20 km from where the route implied, but that anchor is the weak Bareji cluster, so the distance proves little either way - worth a check]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.580950,-9.164520,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Safia</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>CONFIRMED by Will, 4 Oct 2026: there is only one Safia, so this is it - the airstrip at 9d35.70'S 148d38.34'E (Pacific Wrecks). Aiari-Safia is therefore genuinely a 54 km route]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.639000,-9.595000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Sairope</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village; GeoNames has New Sairope 2 km away. Gora &gt; Asafa &gt; Sairope is then a consistent westward chain, which is the corroboration]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.043960,-8.921300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Sigara</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>36 households</b>, zone 6, ward 5<br/>long walk to road (2.5-10 km)<br/>position: field evidence<br/>'the path ends at the main village, but the point is in a hamlet of Sigara. Near, but across a river'. The gazetteer's 148.4491 is the hamlet; 'Track from Kaura to Sigara Village' ends here, 1,281 m west, and this is the main village. The gazetteer's point is kept in bad_positions.csv reasoning only - it is a real hamlet, not an error, but it is not what the list means by Sigara. The third 'Sigara]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.437400,-9.041100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Umuate</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>endpoint of Davids_track_record_from_Itokama_to_Umuate; the gazetteer's Umuwate at 148.4014 is 19 km away and cannot be this place]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.237000,-9.263700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Warisota</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>OSM village beside Embi. AMBIGUOUS: GeoNames has another Warisota 13 km north and OSM a New Warisota 45 km west - this is the one the route fits]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.430320,-8.851710,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    <Placemark><name>Yoivi</name><styleUrl>#field_evidence</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[position: field evidence<br/>village end of the recording 'Yoivi junction to Yoivi village'; the gazetteer carries only Verayame, 500 m west]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.450000,-9.139100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
  </Folder>
